CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ cross-cast to the sibling subobject: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dereferenced function pointer must be.*: FAILURE$
--
N5008 [expr.dynamic.cast]/9.2: dynamic_cast<iface_b *>(p) with p pointing
to the iface_a subobject of an impl object yields a pointer to its iface_b
subobject, so q->b() returns 2.  The front end modelled the check as a
nondeterministic choice between null and the unadjusted pointer (bin53;
the call through it then failed the function-pointer check).  See
cpp98_dynamic_cast_runtime_check.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
